(4875861, 705380, 811, '<td valign="top">great perspective.</td>', 'great perspective.', '2008-08-08 17:21:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(4876058, 706454, 41675, '<td valign="top">Great woody shot! I absolutely love it. Bit blown out by his little feet, but very clever.</td>', 'Great woody shot! I absolutely love it. Bit blown out by his little feet, but very clever.', '2008-08-08 19:21:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(4876164, 706079, 63269, '<td valign="top">Nice lighting - and that reflective surface makes this look really neat! This is totally personal but I wonder how it might have looked with a motion blur on the "falling" leaf? Good photo.</td>', 'Nice lighting - and that reflective surface makes this look really neat! This is totally personal but I wonder how it might have looked with a motion blur on the "falling" leaf? Good photo.', '2008-08-08 21:11:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(4876167, 704780, 63269, '<td valign="top">AWESOME capture! Imo, the colors are just a bit over-saturated. But otherwise this is an amazing image. Makes me want to go for a swim too now! :)</td>', 'AWESOME capture! Imo, the colors are just a bit over-saturated. But otherwise this is an amazing image. Makes me want to go for a swim too now! :)', '2008-08-08 21:13:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(4876171, 706329, 63269, '<td valign="top">IMO the composition is a little cluttered. however, given the apparantly cramped surroundings and the gigantic subject, I know from experience that creating a good composition would indeed be very, <i>very </i>difficult, if not impossible.</td>', 'IMO the composition is a little cluttered. however, given the apparantly cramped surroundings and the gigantic subject, I know from experience that creating a good composition would indeed be very, very difficult, if not impossible.', '2008-08-08 21:16:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(4876174, 706370, 63269, '<td valign="top">Nice composition and colors - those silhouettes are very striking and interesting!</td>', 'Nice composition and colors - those silhouettes are very striking and interesting!', '2008-08-08 21:17:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(4876177, 706468, 63269, '<td valign="top">The focus is sort of half-way inbetween clear and blurred. I don''t mind artistic blur, but personally I feel the photo should be without question one or the other. Granted, I''m sure this was a difficult subject to capture! Also the contrast might be a little high.</td>', 'The focus is sort of half-way inbetween clear and blurred. I don''t mind artistic blur, but personally I feel the photo should be without question one or the other. Granted, I''m sure this was a difficult subject to capture! Also the contrast might be a little high.', '2008-08-08 21:19:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(4876184, 706061, 63269, '<td valign="top">imo the composition is a little weak. instead of placing the subject in the dead center, experiment with using the rule of thirds (or basically placing the subject off in a corner) and also not cropping so tightly. otherwise, your focus, colors, and lighting are good, and this is certainly an interesting subject. Hope this helps! :)</td>', 'imo the composition is a little weak. instead of placing the subject in the dead center, experiment with using the rule of thirds (or basically placing the subject off in a corner) and also not cropping so tightly. otherwise, your focus, colors, and lighting are good, and this is certainly an interesting subject. Hope this helps! :)', '2008-08-08 21:24:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(4876308, 705166, 75034, '<td valign="top">Jason, this is fantastic. Even when she''s supposed to be bad, your wife looks good. I love the lighting on her face and the catch light in her eyes. The PP is just dark enough to have the air of mystery and still light enough to see the stunning features of her face. <br/> <br/>I wish you well with this shot, I hope it gets the support from the voters that it deserves.<br/> <br/>A 10 from me, great work. We have lots of the same gear, if you ever come back to Canada could you teach me how to use it :)<br/> <br/>All the best.<br/> <br/>MAX!</td>', 'Jason, this is fantastic. Even when she''s supposed to be bad, your wife looks good. I love the lighting on her face and the catch light in her eyes. The PP is just dark enough to have the air of mystery and still light enough to see the stunning features of her face.  I wish you well with this shot, I hope it gets the support from the voters that it deserves. A 10 from me, great work. We have lots of the same gear, if you ever come back to Canada could you teach me how to use it :) All the best. MAX!', '2008-08-08 23:07:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(4876373, 705725, 75034, '<td valign="top">Coley, this is a fantastic follow up to your last angel shot <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=698444" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/889/120/698444.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/889/120/698444.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/889/120/698444.jpg"/></a>. I hope this one does just as well as the last one. It''s nice to see the story contunue and you have left it open to ones own imagination. <br/> <br/>I find the shadows interesting, your umbrella does not have one, you have only a small oneand it''s in front of you, about the size of your right leg, your angel''s shadow is an the ground in front of her, the shadow from your right arm cover some of her legs, the bench''s shadow is behind the angel and the balloons have no shadow to speak of. Interesting lighting set up you had out there on the open plain, very interesting indeed.<br/> <br/>I think B&amp;W was a great choice for this shot and the DoF is spot on. I love the contrast and the view in your shot. Great work as per usual coley.<br/> <br/>I should hope to see this one in the top 3. 10 from me.<br/> <br/>MAX!</td>', 'Coley, this is a fantastic follow up to your last angel shot . I hope this one does just as well as the last one. It''s nice to see the story contunue and you have left it open to ones own imagination.  I find the shadows interesting, your umbrella does not have one, you have only a small oneand it''s in front of you, about the size of your right leg, your angel''s shadow is an the ground in front of her, the shadow from your right arm cover some of her legs, the bench''s shadow is behind the angel and the balloons have no shadow to speak of. Interesting lighting set up you had out there on the open plain, very interesting indeed. I think B&W was a great choice for this shot and the DoF is spot on. I love the contrast and the view in your shot. Great work as per usual coley. I should hope to see this one in the top 3. 10 from me. MAX!', '2008-08-08 23:55:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(4876749, 706180, 63633, '<td valign="top">Love it! Has to be Irene :)</td>', 'Love it! Has to be Irene :)', '2008-08-09 08:37:55.000000', NULL, 1),
