(4877992, 705691, 53316, '<td valign="top">Beautiful. I adore this.</td>', 'Beautiful. I adore this.', '2008-08-10 04:18:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878007, 705734, 53316, '<td valign="top">Awwwww. This is processed SO beautifully. I was thinking about this challenge a bit ago and how my mother had given me a dead butterfly so that I could use it as a photo prop if it ever came up. I kept it in a container for a while but when I moved I didn''t take it, and I felt bad that I didn''t have it available to use for this challenge.... But I feel better now, because seeing your butterfly shot is so surpassing what I would have done! :-<br/> <br/>The surreal yellow/green colors in the butterfly and the background are just so gorgeous and the contrast is dramatic and emotional. Great job.</td>', 'Awwwww. This is processed SO beautifully. I was thinking about this challenge a bit ago and how my mother had given me a dead butterfly so that I could use it as a photo prop if it ever came up. I kept it in a container for a while but when I moved I didn''t take it, and I felt bad that I didn''t have it available to use for this challenge.... But I feel better now, because seeing your butterfly shot is so surpassing what I would have done! :- The surreal yellow/green colors in the butterfly and the background are just so gorgeous and the contrast is dramatic and emotional. Great job.', '2008-08-10 04:34:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878008, 705864, 53316, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous colors!</td>', 'Gorgeous colors!', '2008-08-10 04:35:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878010, 705795, 53316, '<td valign="top">I like the processing - great colors and contrast.</td>', 'I like the processing - great colors and contrast.', '2008-08-10 04:35:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878012, 706070, 53316, '<td valign="top">Nice interpretation of the challenge!! And a visually very appealing image.</td>', 'Nice interpretation of the challenge!! And a visually very appealing image.', '2008-08-10 04:36:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878015, 705794, 53316, '<td valign="top">Aside from a tiny bit too much noise for my tastes I LOVE LOVE LOVE this. I think it''s a great interpretation of the challenge - your title helps tie it together but it also works visually, not solely reliant on the title - the composition is great, the colors are superb, and finally (and what a lot of people don''t seem to understand is so important about kinetic shots like this) your contrast is superb. Very well done!</td>', 'Aside from a tiny bit too much noise for my tastes I LOVE LOVE LOVE this. I think it''s a great interpretation of the challenge - your title helps tie it together but it also works visually, not solely reliant on the title - the composition is great, the colors are superb, and finally (and what a lot of people don''t seem to understand is so important about kinetic shots like this) your contrast is superb. Very well done!', '2008-08-10 04:37:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878016, 706354, 53316, '<td valign="top">Wow, the composition here is fantastic!!</td>', 'Wow, the composition here is fantastic!!', '2008-08-10 04:38:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878018, 705750, 53316, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous colors and texture.</td>', 'Gorgeous colors and texture.', '2008-08-10 04:38:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878019, 706189, 53316, '<td valign="top">Very beautiful. I love the colors.</td>', 'Very beautiful. I love the colors.', '2008-08-10 04:38:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878020, 706355, 53316, '<td valign="top">Neat contrast between the rustic foreground and the modern background - for some reason I think it really works!</td>', 'Neat contrast between the rustic foreground and the modern background - for some reason I think it really works!', '2008-08-10 04:39:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878031, 704597, 53316, '<td valign="top">Some people might not see being penitent as related to being fallen but it really does work. The pose with him looking up is perfect. Being advanced editing I will say that the spot in his right eye might have been cloned out as it is a bit distracting. The crop works for me and I love the contrast a lot. Overall a very engaging and emotional image.</td>', 'Some people might not see being penitent as related to being fallen but it really does work. The pose with him looking up is perfect. Being advanced editing I will say that the spot in his right eye might have been cloned out as it is a bit distracting. The crop works for me and I love the contrast a lot. Overall a very engaging and emotional image.', '2008-08-10 04:43:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878032, 706406, 53316, '<td valign="top">Very dramatic lighting!</td>', 'Very dramatic lighting!', '2008-08-10 04:43:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878034, 706389, 53316, '<td valign="top">Oh! How cute! The photographer as the fallen one instead of the subject! Well the challenge didn''t say "portray a fallen subject" did it? LOL, very awesome.</td>', 'Oh! How cute! The photographer as the fallen one instead of the subject! Well the challenge didn''t say "portray a fallen subject" did it? LOL, very awesome.', '2008-08-10 04:44:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878036, 706467, 53316, '<td valign="top">Eerie and beautiful. Gorgeous processing.</td>', 'Eerie and beautiful. Gorgeous processing.', '2008-08-10 04:45:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878041, 706388, 53316, '<td valign="top">Very, very magical.</td>', 'Very, very magical.', '2008-08-10 04:47:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878063, 705725, 42013, '<td valign="top">Signature. It doesn''t leave as many questions to be answered and I find the position of the models inside your frame to be a more static than your previous entries. I don''t think I''m making sense....  Maybe the light is different. NOt sure. I''m going to need to revisit your others to see if it will help me articulate.<br/> <br/>ETA: see what Karmat said below. :) I think that is what I meant.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-08-11 00:16:00.</i></td>', 'Signature. It doesn''t leave as many questions to be answered and I find the position of the models inside your frame to be a more static than your previous entries. I don''t think I''m making sense....  Maybe the light is different. NOt sure. I''m going to need to revisit your others to see if it will help me articulate. ETA: see what Karmat said below. :) I think that is what I meant.', '2008-08-10 05:13:39.000000', '2008-08-11 01:16:00.000000', 1),
(4878065, 706434, 53316, '<td valign="top">Firstly, let me say that I like the contrast here - nice whites and good blacks - and I like the fact that I can read some of the words on the stones. I also love how you have addressed the challenge: to me, this is a good use of the word "fallen".<br/> <br/>It''s so hard to make rows of stones aligned in this fashion look good. I lived for many years across from a veteran''s cemetery with stones just like this, and I know from experience how it is to photograph them. There''s something about them being lined up so straight and alike that makes it difficult.  <br/> <br/>So I am having problems with the composition overall. It seems too tilted to the right. Also, the stone in the foreground being so centered is not as engaging as putting your main element off to the side and up a bit, for example.  It''s a bit hard, too, how that stone is so out of focus.  Being bigger than the rest makes the viewer want to read it.<br/> <br/>If you don''t know that this is a veteran''s cemetery, it could be hard to tell, as you took the shot from the "back" of the stones. I understand that it could have been an issue with not being able to shoot from the other way or something like that - but I do think the shot would have been more engaging seeing the actual soldier''s names.  Or, you could have had your title be something different (the "soldiers" part leads me to expect soldiers names and not a lot of "his wife") but I do not think that would hav ethe same impact.<br/> <br/>One last thing - I know that when faced with so many gravestones of soldiers, it is a bit overwhelming to think of what they went through, and you might be tempted to capture the enormity of that in sheer numbers. However, getting closer to the subject, capturing fewer stones, may help it be more dramatic and emotional for your viewer.<br/> <br/>I have been a bit harsh but I don''t want you to think I hate the shot. In fact, it is a rare shot that can lead me to be so connected to it that I want to comment at such length.  The image has a lot of potential and if you get the chance to shoot at that location again I would be so interested in seeing further photos!</td>', 'Firstly, let me say that I like the contrast here - nice whites and good blacks - and I like the fact that I can read some of the words on the stones. I also love how you have addressed the challenge: to me, this is a good use of the word "fallen". It''s so hard to make rows of stones aligned in this fashion look good. I lived for many years across from a veteran''s cemetery with stones just like this, and I know from experience how it is to photograph them. There''s something about them being lined up so straight and alike that makes it difficult.   So I am having problems with the composition overall. It seems too tilted to the right. Also, the stone in the foreground being so centered is not as engaging as putting your main element off to the side and up a bit, for example.  It''s a bit hard, too, how that stone is so out of focus.  Being bigger than the rest makes the viewer want to read it. If you don''t know that this is a veteran''s cemetery, it could be hard to tell, as you took the shot from the "back" of the stones. I understand that it could have been an issue with not being able to shoot from the other way or something like that - but I do think the shot would have been more engaging seeing the actual soldier''s names.  Or, you could have had your title be something different (the "soldiers" part leads me to expect soldiers names and not a lot of "his wife") but I do not think that would hav ethe same impact. One last thing - I know that when faced with so many gravestones of soldiers, it is a bit overwhelming to think of what they went through, and you might be tempted to capture the enormity of that in sheer numbers. However, getting closer to the subject, capturing fewer stones, may help it be more dramatic and emotional for your viewer. I have been a bit harsh but I don''t want you to think I hate the shot. In fact, it is a rare shot that can lead me to be so connected to it that I want to comment at such length.  The image has a lot of potential and if you get the chance to shoot at that location again I would be so interested in seeing further photos!', '2008-08-10 05:21:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878219, 706468, 67258, '<td valign="top">The tilt helps the idea of a potential fall.  The lack of clarity on the horse and rider is a problem for the success of the photo - panning with the rider, or a faster shutter speed would help in the future.</td>', 'The tilt helps the idea of a potential fall.  The lack of clarity on the horse and rider is a problem for the success of the photo - panning with the rider, or a faster shutter speed would help in the future.', '2008-08-10 08:45:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(4878220, 706427, 67258, '<td valign="top">Quite a nice composition, but the lack of detail in the duck detracts - I would prefer either stronger silhouette image, or else spot-metering from the duck so that it is more fully exposed.</td>', 'Quite a nice composition, but the lack of detail in the duck detracts - I would prefer either stronger silhouette image, or else spot-metering from the duck so that it is more fully exposed.', '2008-08-10 08:47:44.000000', NULL, 1),
