(4879918, 706180, 52549, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by paladin_online:</b></div><hr/><i> Hi Irene, congratz on the score!  I like this style a lot.  I''ve looked at some of your other shots and gathered that you did this on a glass table with a blue transparency over one flash from underneath, but how did you get the back to be glass too...?  Looks like a curved product table made of glass/mirror?  Or if you''ve already explained this in another shot, could you please point me to it?  Thanks very much! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Sure, no problem. It''s a small piece of dark tinted glass propped up on four tumblers. The glass is lit from beneath and from behind. I didn''t use any transparencies. The tinted glass actually gave this cyen hue when lit from underneath (which was fine with me ;-)</td>', 'Originally posted by paladin_online: Hi Irene, congratz on the score!  I like this style a lot.  I''ve looked at some of your other shots and gathered that you did this on a glass table with a blue transparency over one flash from underneath, but how did you get the back to be glass too...?  Looks like a curved product table made of glass/mirror?  Or if you''ve already explained this in another shot, could you please point me to it?  Thanks very much!  Sure, no problem. It''s a small piece of dark tinted glass propped up on four tumblers. The glass is lit from beneath and from behind. I didn''t use any transparencies. The tinted glass actually gave this cyen hue when lit from underneath (which was fine with me ;-)', '2008-08-11 05:53:29.000000', NULL, 0),
