(4880762, 706347, 60173, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by drydoc:</b></div><hr/><i> White on white is sooo hard to do. The front left is the neat part of your image.  The right is too blown out. Was wondering why you did not crop it out. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It''s actually a bright yellow flower that I desaturated 90%ish. I kept the right side, because that''s the stem of the flower. Had it not been a Fallen challenge, I probably would have cropped it out.</td>', 'Originally posted by drydoc: White on white is sooo hard to do. The front left is the neat part of your image.  The right is too blown out. Was wondering why you did not crop it out.   It''s actually a bright yellow flower that I desaturated 90%ish. I kept the right side, because that''s the stem of the flower. Had it not been a Fallen challenge, I probably would have cropped it out.', '2008-08-11 15:01:09.000000', NULL, 0),
